<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cortes of Castile</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corte">Cortes</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> were the representative assembly of the kingdom, made up of the clergy, nobles and representatives of the towns. Rooted in royal councils that admitted townsmen from the late twelfth century, they voted taxes, swore allegiance to heirs and presented petitions. From the sixteenth century only eighteen cities sent deputies, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cortes">Cortes</a> mainly approved taxes such as the millones for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> crown.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cortes-of-castile.jpg" alt="Cortes of Castile" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Danielmoreno4774 · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Senado_de_Espa%C3%B1a_-_XV_legislatura_31-08-2024.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
